build
# Regenerated by Next on every dev start and every build, and the two write
# different contents (".next/dev/types" vs ".next/types"), so a tracked copy is
# dirty within seconds of touching the app. That churn has already blocked a
# `git stash pop` and a branch switch mid-debug. tsc does not need the file —
# typecheck passes on a checkout without it — so nothing is lost by letting Next
# own it.
next-env.d.ts
.DS_Store
*.pem
.env
.env.local
.env*.local
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
.vercel
coverage

